diff --git a/Changelog.md b/Changelog.md
index 5517cf3..d9b5b51 100644
--- a/Changelog.md
+++ b/Changelog.md
@@ -1,3 +1,14 @@
+# Unreleased
+
+- Removed `Zip::Entry#name_safe?`. It was undocumented (`:nodoc:`), nothing in the library called it, and after its own `cleanpath.relative?` guard the rest of it rejected nothing, so it answered `true` for every relative name including `C:/evil.txt`. Containment during extraction is decided by `Entry#extract`, which resolves the destination and refuses a name that leaves it - including through a symlink, which `name_safe?` said in as many words that it could not handle.
+
+- Extraction now raises `Zip::ExtractionError` when the filesystem refuses an entry's name - too long, carrying a byte it cannot hold, or needing a directory that is already a file - where `Errno::ENAMETOOLONG`, `Errno::EEXIST` and `ArgumentError` used to escape. A `destination_directory` the caller got wrong is answered in one of three ways: one that does not exist, or sits under a path this process cannot traverse, still reports with the operating system's own error; one that is not a directory is refused by the containment check, so nothing is written and nothing is raised; and one that is a directory this process cannot write into or cannot traverse raises `Zip::ExtractionError`.
+- A failed extraction no longer damages the destination. Entry contents are written beside the destination and moved into place once complete, so a corrupt archive no longer truncates the file it was overwriting or leaves a partial one behind.
+- An entry whose local header is missing, unreadable, or belongs to a different entry is now refused with a `Zip::Error`. Previously the first two read as an empty payload and the third returned the other entry's contents, all without an error or a warning.
+- A central directory record that runs past the end of the central directory is now refused. Previously it returned an entry whose name was whatever bytes followed the record.
+- An archive truncated inside a local header's name, and an empty buffer passed to `Zip::File.open_buffer`, now raise `Zip::Error` rather than `NoMethodError` and `TypeError`.
+- `Zip::InputStream` now raises `Zip::Error` when a local entry header will not parse and the position still carries a local entry signature, since the archive is declaring an entry it cannot deliver. In 3.6.0 the read simply ended there, with no error and no warning, so an application rejecting malformed archives with `rescue Zip::Error` received a truncated entry list as though the archive had reached its end. Bytes that are neither an entry nor an end-of-central-directory record now end the read with a warning, which is also new here, because the entries beyond them are unreachable either way.
+
 # 3.6.0 (2026-09-01)
 
 - Forward options from OutputStream.open without a block. [#674](https://github.com/rubyzip/rubyzip/pull/674)
